<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gundobad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 516</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gundobad was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundians">Burgundians</a> from about 473 to 516, after serving as a Roman general and briefly as kingmaker in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, where he raised Glycerius to the throne in 473. In his kingdom in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a> valley he issued the law code known as the Lex Burgundionum for his Burgundian subjects and a separate Roman code for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallo-romans">Gallo-Romans</a>. He remained an Arian but tolerated the Catholic Church.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gundobad.jpg" alt="Gundobad" width="320" height="595" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Codex · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gondebaud_par_Roger_Ferrier_Place_du_bourg_de_Four.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
